# APPENDIX

## §A1 Verified root causes (source-anchored)

### Problem B — second response overwrites first

| # | Fact | Source |
|---|---|---|
**🚨 v3: facts corrected to the LIVE transport (`/ws/manager`), not the unused `/ws/agent` AF-webui bridge.**

| B-F1 | The turn produced **two** assistant rounds on disk (SOP-entry text at 203746, Phase-0a-two-tools at 203807). Both exist; only the second shows in the UI. | the turn_002 directory listing |
| B-F2 (v3) | The live chat transport is **`/ws/manager`** (`useManagerChat.js:40`; `setupProxy.js:24`). The `/ws/agent` AF-webui bridge (`agent_service_bridge.py`) is **NOT used** by OpenStartup chat. | useManagerChat.js:40; setupProxy.js:24 |
| B-F3 (v3) | On the manager transport, `message_end` **already carries `message_id`** (half-wired). But `token`, `pending_input`, `message_start` do **NOT** — emitted in `websocket_interactive.py` without it. | manager_websocket_routes.py:512-514; websocket_interactive.py:201,214,314,380 |
| B-F4 | The UI already commits a finished bubble at `message_end` keyed on `data.message_id` (timestamp fallback). The `pending_input` handler **already commits** the prior round's bubble. | useManagerChat.js:384,266 |
| B-F5 | The `message_id` is **not minted per round** — without a per-round id on `token`/`message_start`, the UI's single streaming buffer is overwritten when round 2 starts. | conversational_inferencer.py (no `_current_message_id`); websocket_interactive.py emit sites |
| B-F6 (v3) | A round seam **already exists**: `conversational_inferencer.py:397` fires `send_turn_boundary(...)`; the UI has a `turn_boundary` handler at `useManagerChat.js:410`. This is the hook to mint+carry the per-round id. | conversational_inferencer.py:397; useManagerChat.js:410 |

**Conclusion (B), v3:** Problem B is **half-wired on the correct transport**, not absent on a bridge. Fix: mint `{message_id, round_index}` **per round** at the existing `send_turn_boundary` seam (`conversational_inferencer.py:397`); thread `message_id` through `token`/`pending_input`/`message_start` in **`websocket_interactive.py`** (and per-round on `message_end` in `manager_websocket_routes.py`); UI keys each streaming bubble by `message_id`, committing the prior one and de-duping (the `pending_input` path already commits — key by `message_id` so no double-commit). **No edits to `agent_service_bridge.py` (dead code for this app).**

### Problem A — multiple tools not shown as tabs

| # | Fact | Source |
|---|---|---|
| A-F1 | When >1 tool is emitted **in one round**, the server already builds a single compound widget: InputModeConfig(mode=FREE_TEXT, metadata={compound: True, tools: tool_configs}). | conversational_inferencer.py:2373-2378 |
| A-F2 | Each tool_configs[i] carries tool_type, prompt, input_mode, output_var, expected_input_type, prefix. Order preserved (list). | conversational_inferencer.py:2362-2369 |
| A-F3 | The parser preserves tool order but has **no parallel_group/group field** today. | conversation_response_parser.py (grep parallel_group/group → none) |
| A-F4 | There is **no React component** that renders metadata.compound===true as tabs (grep compound/Tabs in chat UI → only unrelated MUI Tabs in popovers). | OpenStartup/.../ui/src grep |
| A-F5 | The widget dispatcher routes by metadata.widget_type or mode (precedent: proposal_selection, confirmation, path_input). A compound/tabbed widget can follow the same widget_type dispatch. | typed-input plan §D6 F10; registerBuiltins.js |

**Conclusion (A):** tabbed rendering is **partially server-ready** (compound metadata exists for same-round multi-tool) but (1) the UI never renders it as tabs, and (2) the LLM cannot *express* grouping intent. Feature needs: a parallel_group field (parser + model), server grouping logic, a widget_type "compound_tabbed" signal, and a React tabbed widget.

### Problem C — one user request becomes two turn directories

| # | Fact | Source |
|---|---|---|
| C-F1 | `turn_001/turn.json` holds `user_input: "help improve the model for responsible ai"` but `rendered_prompt: ""` and **no `RovoDevCliInferencer/` rounds**. | turn_001/turn.json |
| C-F2 | `turn_002/` holds **two** `RovoDevCliInferencer-…` round dirs (203746, 203807) but **no `turn.json`/user_input**. | turn_002 listing |
| C-F3 | The UI numbers turns by **counting `turn_` directories**: `new_style = sum(1 for p in session_dir.iterdir() if p.name.startswith("turn_") …)`. Two dirs → "2 turns". | conversation_service.py:506-508 |
| C-F4 | `save_turn_data` writes the user input under **`turn_{new_turn}`** (e.g. turn_001). | conversation_service.py:~610 (step 2) |
| C-F5 | The streaming `cache_folder` is rotated to **`turn_{new_turn + 1}`** (e.g. turn_002) — a **different anchor** for the same turn. | conversation_service.py:624 (step 4) |
| C-F6 | `_on_new_turn` (which runs step 2 + step 4) fires **per agentic-loop boundary**, including a **pre-loop** call at `start_iteration==0` and again after **each widget handoff** — NOT once per user message. | conversational_inferencer.py:371 (pre-loop), :568 (post-widget) |
| C-F7 | The pre-loop `cache_folder` is set to `turn_{initial_turn+1}` (turn_001) at line 633, but the immediately-following pre-loop `_fire_new_turn` (line 371) runs step 4 and **repoints it to turn_002** — so the next iteration of the SAME response streams into turn_002. | conversation_service.py:633; conversational_inferencer.py:371; conversation_service.py:624 |

**Conclusion (C-1):** two compounding bugs. **C-1a (off-by-one anchor):** `save_turn_data(new_turn)` and `cache_folder(new_turn+1)` disagree, so a turn's user input and its response land in different directories. **C-1b (granularity):** the turn directory advances per agentic-loop iteration (incl. the pre-loop init and every widget handoff), not per user message — conflating "loop iteration" with "conversational turn" (the same root family as Problem B). Fix: advance the turn directory **once per user message**, and make the response co-locate with its own user input (same anchor).

### Problem C-2 — assistant response never persisted as a message + stale index (NEW in v2; both v1 and Codex missed it)

| # | Fact | Source |
|---|---|---|
| C2-F1 | The WS route appends the assistant message **once** at loop end via `final_content` (built by blocking on `run_conversation_turn`); intermediate rounds are never persisted as messages. | manager_websocket_routes.py:423,429,469 |
| C2-F2 | `session_store.append_message` (used via `data_svc.append_message`, data_service.py:670-671) calls `_persist_session` but **NOT `_update_index()`** — so `sessions_index.message_count` goes stale. | session_store.py:334-345 (no `_update_index`); session_store.py:681 (where `_update_index` lives) |
| C2-F3 | Symptom: the session list showed **"1 msgs"** (stale index count) while the chat header showed "3 messages" (welcome + user + assistant) — exactly the staleness predicted by C2-F2. | observed UI + session_state.json |

**Conclusion (C-2):** (a) persist each round's assistant text as its own message at the round boundary (not one `final_content` at the very end), tagged `{turn_number, round_index, message_id}`; (b) make `append_message` call `_update_index()` so the index stays correct. C-2 is why the assistant turn appeared to "not exist" in the session list even though it streamed on screen.

## §A2 Follow-ups (out of scope here)

- **F-consolidate:** dormant handler-registry vs. live inline _build_input_mode split (tracked in typed-input plan §A4.1) — this plan also touches the live inline path; consolidation remains separate.
- **Concurrent interactive tabs with independent submit:** this plan renders grouped tools in tabs but submits them as one compound payload. True per-tab async submit is deferred.

## §A3 Risks

| # | Risk | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|
| R1 | Adding message_id changes the WS contract; an out-of-date UI would ignore it | message_id is additive; UI already falls back to Date.now(). Server stays backward-compatible. |
| R2 | Per-round bubbles could double-render the final message if both pending_input (commit) and message_end fire for the same id | Key both commit paths by message_id; a bubble with a given message_id is committed at most once (UI reducer guard). |
| R3 | parallel_group semantics could confuse the LLM | Explicit Response-Format guidance + examples; default (omitted group) = "consecutive tools may be shown together" so existing SOPs improve without edits. |
| R4 | Tabbed compound submit must still bind every tool's output_var (incl. composite nested inputs from typed-input plan) | Reuse the compound collection + finalize_input_value chokepoint; test that a tabbed group binds all output vars. |

