### §A4.1 If forced to pick ONE plan among the 3 (v4 — answer)

**Honest answer: Claude's `update-…-goose.md` (its latest version) is the best independent analysis; THIS v4 is the best document to execute from.** I keep pointing at Claude's plan for the *analysis* crown because, across the last two rounds, it twice caught load-bearing errors in my own plan — and I verified every one against live source:

* **Round 3:** it alone had the right **transport** (`/ws/manager`, not the `/ws/agent` `agent_service_bridge` my v1/v2 targeted — dead code).
* **Round 4 (this round):** it caught **three more** real issues in my v3 — (a) the **round-seam** error (minting id at the turn-gated `send_turn_boundary`, which misses action-tool continuation rounds `5a/5b` and stops firing once Problem C makes turn advance per-message); (b) **Problem A inverted** (CompoundWidget is the lossless, wired one — my "rewire dead+lossy MultiInputWidget" was backwards); (c) **mint-in-AF would NameError** (`uuid` not imported in AF). It also surfaced a genuinely new bug both my plan and the original Claude plan missed: **widget card lost on reload** (now Commit 11).

**Why execute from v4 (this file) anyway:** v4 absorbs *all* of Claude's verified corrections **and** improves on them with the things my document does better — (i) reuse the **existing** `_fire_turn_complete` per-iteration signal as round-complete (Claude/X add a redundant new hook), (ii) a **typed `RoundContext`** rather than a loose dict that implicitly mutates `cache_folder` (the implicit coupling that caused the original turn-split), (iii) the **verified direct-map** payload (my finding — X over-mandates cosmetic `{values}`), plus my 3-tier structure, 12-commit checklist, risk register, and anchor preflight.

* **Codex/X** contributed the right *ideas first* (dedicated round lifecycle, widget-card persistence, buffer reset, index staleness) and deserves real credit for the round-lifecycle insight — but remains the lightest on file:line anchors / execution detail.

**Net:** for the **single best reasoning artifact**, Claude's plan earned it (it caught my mistakes twice). For the **single doc to hand an implementer**, use **v4** — it is now fact-aligned with Claude's plan and richer in execution scaffolding. The three plans have **converged**: same model, same transport, same seam, same widget, same payload.
